                <pb facs="0749" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv12/pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 181.9202/178: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Bandholtz to
                        the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Budapest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-07">October 7, 1919</date>.<lb/>[Received October 7—5:57
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>128. For Polk from Bandholtz. Seals on museum doors are as yet undisturbed.
                    Roumanians have delivered 1,000 serviceable rifles for the police. Evacuation of
                    western Hungary should end today. Colonel Moore has reported and order will be
                    issued at once returning Colonel Horowitz to Paris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bandholtz</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
